childcare requirement in the CHIPS Act is recognition and funding at the federal level that parents cannot work without childcare. This is not going to be the last time that childcare is included as a provision of receiving funding. Mark my words!\n\nIf you want to learn more about the childcare landscape and the best ways to help your employees with childcare, I’d love to connect!', 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '8mo', 'last_updated': '2024-08-07 16:30:55', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 667197516, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7212083296418062336', 'followers': None, 'date': '1mo', 'description': 'What an honor to be invited to the US Chamber of Commerce today on behalf of Winnie for the first National Child Care Innovation Summit.\n\nWe started this company over 8 years ago when everyone said the TAM was too small and our idea was too niche. Our “niche company” has the attention of the US government now. LFG!', 'reactions_count': 207, 'comments_count': 16, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-09-07 12:11:48', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 667197517, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7198711005210632192', 'followers': None, 'date': '2mo', 'description': '“Child care facilities are being forced to either find alternative business models to pay the bills or shut down,” said Sara Mauskopf, CEO and co-founder at one of the largest online child care marketplaces\xa0Winnie. \n\n👉 Read more here https://lnkd.in/g5-DYkPB', 'reactions_count': 4, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-09-07 12:11:48', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 667197518, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7190871841643663360', 'followers': None, 'date': '3mo', 'description': 'Price transparency increases enrollment rates by 33% for childcare centers!', 'reactions_count': 22, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': "Imagine not knowing the rent for an apartment until you showed up and toured it. One thing child care providers get wrong is that it's better to withhold any pricing information until a parent tours their center. We have data from Winnie to show that keeping prices a secret is hurting childcare businesses by increasing operational costs and lowering enrollment rates. \n\nIn the competitive world of childcare, transparency isn't just a good practice—it's a strategic advantage. Sharing pricing upfront not only improves search rankings and increases parental interest, but it also leads to a 33% increase in enrollment rates for centers that do so. \n\nIt's an outdated practice to keep prices hidden and it's disadvantaging the entire childcare industry as well as families. Hopefully by sharing the business impact we can advocate for more price transparency in childcare https://lnkd.in/gCgAaHj6", 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '3mo', 'last_updated': '2024-09-07 12:11:48', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 667197519, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7189842402948386817', 'followers': None, 'date': '3mo', 'description': 'Miss our group chat with Sara Mauskopf from Winnie earlier this week?\n\nThis was a really great group chat with with Sara where we she shared some of her key learnings from Postmates, the founding story for Winnie, what the first steps were that they took to start it as an app for parents to discover activities for kids nearby, what led to their pivot into childcare, we did a deep dive into it as a leading childcare marketplace today, got to learn more about their recent growth, and also had a great group Q&A.\n\nThe recording is now live!\n\nhttps://lnkd.in/gH_sB_7g', 'reactions_count': 7, 'comments_count': 1, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-09-07 12:11:48', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 667197520, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7189300090006614017', 'followers': None, 'date': '3mo', 'description': "I've been a speaker at the ASU+GSV Summit for many years, but this year's panel stood out as my favorite because WE WENT THERE and had a lively debate around some controversial topics in early education like funding models, the impact of AI, and the role the government should play.\n\nI had the honor of speaking alongside brilliant leaders like Chris Bennett (Wonderschool), John Olsen (Teaching Strategies, LLC), Ben Newton (Vivvi), and Matt Greenfield (Rethink Education). The panel was about innovative solutions for making high-quality early childhood education both accessible and affordable.\n\nWe delved into the controversial topic of whether a private versus public funding model best serves the future of early education. We talked about how society undervalues early education and (IMHO) overvalues higher ed. And some of us disagreed about how AI can/should transform childcare. Check out the full discussion here:", 'reactions_count': 49, 'comments_count': 3, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-09-07 12:11:48', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 667197521, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7166943276225290240', 'followers': None, 'date': '5mo', 'description': "If you're an employer interested in providing a childcare benefit that's far more affordable and flexible than an onsite center, we'd love to talk! https://lnkd.in/gFTEqEA4", 'reactions_count': 7, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': "Not sure if people saw this amid all the layoff news, but Google and other companies have closed their onsite childcare centers.\n\nGoogle cited cost-cutting as the reason and General Mills cited a post-pandemic drop in usage as families preferred closer options. \n\nCompanies that sell child care benefits to employers should think outside the box in terms of what solutions they offer. A one size fits all approach like an onsite center isn't going to work when workers are distributed, or when cost is a concern. And if cost is a concern for a trillion dollar company like Google, trust me it is for every company.\n\nAt Winnie, we're betting that employers who want to provide childcare benefits will look to solutions that are more flexible and take advantage of the existing supply of child care providers, rather than trying to stand up entirely new centers. Time will tell if we're right!", 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '5mo', 'last_updated': '2024-09-07 12:11:48', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 667197522, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7150668728257445888', 'followers': None, 'date': '7mo', 'description': 'Winnie’s CEO Sara Mauskopf spoke at CES on the importance of childcare to help moms and all parents return to the workforce after having a baby 🤗', 'reactions_count': 4, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'The Female Quotient', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/femalequotient', 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': 'The healthcare industry and workplaces across the U.S. have largely overlooked ne