eryville, a beautiful campus caring for kids from 12 weeks to 6 years old - the perfect spot to talk about the importance of childcare and how it's critical infrastructure for mothers and families.\n\nI left the discussion feeling so invigorated. First, it was awesome to hear about how Guidepost has built so many thriving childcare centers (~150!) across the country and world. The news contains so much doom and gloom about the childcare industry but here's a model that supports families, teachers, and provides a great foundation for children. So many awesome businesses like this exist and are thriving!\n\nSecond, it was great to get so much support from the public sector. I was told by the First Partner how much California values innovation in the private sector and how much the govenor's office wants to collaborate with Winnie and see the company thrive. Wow that felt good!", 'reactions_count': 76, 'comments_count': 3, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-11-26 20:15:23', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 789170347, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7226989590018940929', 'followers': None, 'date': '2mo', 'description': "Today we launched a childcare cost calculator at Winnie to show just how much childcare costs based on where you live: https://lnkd.in/gPzaYSy5 Childcare is clearly expensive, but even more so when you take a pay cut just for becoming a mother.\n\nToday is #MomsEqualPay day, the day that raises awareness of the pay penalty mothers experience in the workplace. At Winnie, we are committed to paying our employees fairly, no matter their parenthood status. That's why we have taken the Equal Pay Pledge, reaffirming our dedication to closing the pay gap and ensuring fair compensation for all employees.\n\nRead more here about how you can take the equal pay pledge, and why childcare might FEEL more expensive than it really is when moms simultaneously take a pay cut just as they need to pay for care. https://lnkd.in/gnhRFWVY", 'reactions_count': 160, 'comments_count': 6, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-11-26 20:15:23', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 789170348, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7212083296418062336', 'followers': None, 'date': '4mo', 'description': 'What an honor to be invited to the US Chamber of Commerce today on behalf of Winnie for the first National Child Care Innovation Summit.\n\nWe started this company over 8 years ago when everyone said the TAM was too small and our idea was too niche. Our “niche company” has the attention of the US government now. LFG!', 'reactions_count': 206, 'comments_count': 16, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-11-26 20:15:23', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 789170349, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7198711005210632192', 'followers': None, 'date': '5mo', 'description': '“Child care facilities are being forced to either find alternative business models to pay the bills or shut down,” said Sara Mauskopf, CEO and co-founder at one of the largest online child care marketplaces\xa0Winnie. \n\n👉 Read more here https://lnkd.in/g5-DYkPB', 'reactions_count': 4, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-11-26 20:15:23', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 789170350, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7190871841643663360', 'followers': None, 'date': '6mo', 'description': 'Price transparency increases enrollment rates by 33% for childcare centers!', 'reactions_count': 22, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': "Imagine not knowing the rent for an apartment until you showed up and toured it. One thing child care providers get wrong is that it's better to withhold any pricing information until a parent tours their center. We have data from Winnie to show that keeping prices a secret is hurting childcare businesses by increasing operational costs and lowering enrollment rates. \n\nIn the competitive world of childcare, transparency isn't just a good practice—it's a strategic advantage. Sharing pricing upfront not only improves search rankings and increases parental interest, but it also leads to a 33% increase in enrollment rates for centers that do so. \n\nIt's an outdated practice to keep prices hidden and it's disadvantaging the entire childcare industry as well as families. Hopefully by sharing the business impact we can advocate for more price transparency in childcare https://lnkd.in/gCgAaHj6", 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '6mo', 'last_updated': '2024-11-26 20:15:23', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 789170351, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7189842402948386817', 'followers': None, 'date': '6mo', 'description': 'Miss our group chat with Sara Mauskopf from Winnie earlier this week?\n\nThis was a really great group chat with with Sara where we she shared some of her key learnings from Postmates, the founding story for Winnie, what the first steps were that they took to start it as an app for parents to discover activities for kids nearby, what led to their pivot into childcare, we did a deep dive into it as a leading childcare marketplace today, got to learn more about their recent growth, and also had a great group Q&A.\n\nThe recording is now live!\n\nhttps://lnkd.in/gH_sB_7g', 'reactions_count': 7, 'comments_count': 1, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-11-26 20:15:23', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 820553413, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7240394983441059840', 'followers': None, 'date': '2mo', 'description': 'Childcare & Remote Work\n\nRemote work has reshaped childcare needs, but not always for the better, especially for those balancing career and caregiving.\n\nWinnie’s Sara Mauskopf and Alex Wilhelm break it down:\n\nRecent data shows women aged 25-44 are more likely to work remotely than men, driven by a need to juggle childcare - often at the cost of career progression.\n\nAccording to the Bureau of Labor Statistics:\n-- Women 25 to 34 are 28% remote\n-- Women 35 to 44 are 30% remote\n-- 7-8% higher than men in the same demographic', 'reactions_count': 39, 'comments_count': 8, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-01-03 08:39:39', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 820553414, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7240142811113648129', 'followers': None, 'date': '2mo', 'description': "The Call for Innovation in Childcare\n\nThe childcare market has a massive TAM but still lacks competition and innovation. Winnie is stepping up to improve the industry for parents, kids, and caregivers.\n\nWith a $60B market, there's room for new players.\n\nAnd it's not just about profit; it's about improving the future for parents, kids, and caregivers.", 'reactions_count': 56, 'comments_count': 13, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_