 1}, {'id': 1021138593, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7305218790366027776', 'followers': None, 'date': '1mo', 'description': 'In a recent Forbes article, Sara Mauskopf underscores the growing demand for providers to deliver more than just daycare. “With parents becoming more selective and competition among [childcare] providers increasing, standing out requires more than just having open spots—it demands differentiation, strong marketing and a commitment to delivering high-quality education.”\n\xa0\nToday’s parents are more discerning than ever. They’re looking for intentional learning environments that set them up for success.\n\xa0\nLearning Care Group is embracing this shift. We focus on early childhood learning and education, offering a research-backed curriculum designed to foster cognitive, social, and emotional growth. We’re working to ensure every child leaves our program not just ready for kindergarten, but ready for life.\n\xa0\nRead Sara Mauskopf’s full article here:', 'reactions_count': 80, 'comments_count': 4, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138594, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7302790202194898945', 'followers': 2989, 'date': '1mo', 'description': None, 'reactions_count': 8, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': "AI is transforming industries at an unprecedented pace. We see it writing code, streamlining operations, and even making complex decisions. But amidst all the well deserved hype, one thing is becoming even clearer: the roles that require humans are more valuable than ever.\n\nChildcare and early education are prime examples. While AI can help providers, it cannot replace them. Teaching, nurturing, and fostering social-emotional growth in young children requires a physical human presence. \n\nI shared this as one of 30 leaders of the care economy who contributed to The Holding Co.'s 2025 Care Trends: https://lnkd.in/gK7igMYk  This report combines insight from founders, investors, public sector leaders, and more on what’s happening in care today. The section in AI is one I find particularly interesting.\n\nAs more industries embrace AI, we’ll see a shift in how society values work. I believe jobs that require interpersonal relationships will not only remain irreplaceable but will become more respected and better compensated as their scarcity and importance grow. \n\nAt Winnie, we see firsthand how essential childcare providers are as both educators and as the foundation that enables parents to work and economies to function. As AI reshapes the future of work, I'm hopeful we will recognize and invest in the people who do the jobs that AI never can.", 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '1mo', 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138595, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7302472846671237120', 'followers': 46863, 'date': '1mo', 'description': 'What was once a supply-constrained market where any open spot would be taken is now demand-driven, where providers compete to stand out. Read more: https://hubs.li/Q038ZvQM0\n\nPost written by Sara Mauskopf, Forbes Councils Member.', 'reactions_count': 13, 'comments_count': 2, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138596, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7293006872582701056', 'followers': 130, 'date': '2mo', 'description': 'Here at EarlyJ, we keep our finger on the pulse of current trends in early childhood education. That’s why we were thrilled to recently host a webinar with Sara Mauskopf, CEO and Co-founder of Winnie — a platform that helps millions of parents discover high-quality daycare and preschool options and empowers preschool providers with the tools to grow their businesses. Sara spoke with Bay Area Jewish preschools about how to harness market trends and technology to improve their programming and strengthen their business models. Thank you, Sara, for sharing your expertise! We look forward to hosting more events in response to our local preschools’ needs.\n\n#BayArea #EarlyJ #Impact #NonProfit #JewishEducation #JewishCommunity #JewishNonProfit #EarlyChildhoodEducation #Education #CommunityEngagement #JewishCommunity #Webinar', 'reactions_count': 15, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138597, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7288259848893280257', 'followers': 823, 'date': '2mo', 'description': "As a network of Early Childhood Education professionals, there's one truth we've learned: different generations have different childcare needs. What are the needs of Millennial and Gen Z parents? What can we do as providers to meet these needs? \n\nIt was a pleasure to sit down with Sara Mauskopf, CEO and Co-Founder of Winnie, to discuss the shifting needs of today's parents and how childcare providers can meet them: https://bit.ly/4g0sGmt\n\n#ECE #Childcare", 'reactions_count': 11, 'comments_count': 1, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138598, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7279990699620495360', 'followers': 2989, 'date': '3mo', 'description': 'This year Winnie helped a record number of families find the childcare they need! Over 659K parents found child care on Winnie with 153K different child care providers across the United States. \n\nTo put this in perspective, there are\xa013.7M households\xa0with children under 6 in the United States.\xa063% of these households\xa0have all parents in the workforce\xa0which means there are 8.6M potential buyers of childcare. Of these families,\xa035% use no form of paid childcare\xa0which leaves us with 6M households paying for childcare in 2024 in the US. We helped place over 10% of these households with their childcare arrangement!\n\nHere’s a sneak peak into what’s ahead in 2025 https://lnkd.in/g3PmFaiU', 'reactions_count': 10, 'comments_count': 1, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138599, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7240394983441059840', 'followers': None, 'date': '7mo', 'description': 'Childcare & Remote Work\n\nRemote work has reshaped childcare needs, but not always for the better, especially for those balancing career and caregiving.\n\nWinnie’s Sara Mauskopf and Alex Wilhelm break it down:\n\nRecent data shows women aged 25-44 are more likely to work remotely than men, driven by a need to juggle childcare - often at the cost of career progression.\n\nAccording to the Bureau of Labor Statistics:\n-- Women 25 to 34 are 28% remote\n-- Women 35 to 44 are 30% remote\n-- 7-8% higher than men in the same demographic', 'reactions_count': 41, 'comments_count': 8, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1061917100, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7323517852173393921', 'followers': None, 'date': '1w', 'description': "Mark Zuckerberg is the subject of some outrage. This time he’s in the news for shutting down The Primary School, a free school for low-income Bay Area families, just a few miles from Meta HQ. It offered preschool through 8th grade.\n\nI don’t usually pay close attention to drama around billionaire tech titans, but this one hit differently. A school is closing. Hundreds of families are affected. Zuckerberg called it an experiment that didn’t work out.\n\nExperiments fail all the time in tech. We A/B test, we iterate, we move on. But children aren’t experiments. When kids are in the balance, we don’t get to just walk away.\n\nThis is why the work we’re doing at Winnie takes time. We’ve been at it for almost a decade. I see others in this space raising big capital and trying to scale fast. Too often, families and educators are left behind when the model doesn't work.\n\nWe’re in this for the long haul. Kids and families deserve more than short-term experiments.", 'reactions_count': 1084, 'comments_count': 87, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-06-08 05:25:11', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1061917101, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7318996802345517056', 'followers': 3386, 'date': '3w', 'description': 'Behind the scenes of our expansion to K-12 school search 👀', 'reactions_count': 9, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': 'I posted a month ago about having trouble getting press for a big launch we had coming up of Winnie\'s K-12 school search. Based on the advice of many of you, we decided to shift gears and instead just use channels we had available to get the message out. I’m now convinced that the days of holding news for the press are over.\n\nHere are some of the ways we got the word out: We submitted a Forbes article related to the launch, I went on the Edtech Insiders podcast, and we announced the news on our own blog and social media channels (including this one right here!). We asked some folks that had email lists and audiences to rebroadcast our news. Soon we’ll be sending out emails to our own audience promoting the expansion to K-12.\n\nSo far it’s been working just as well as any "official press" would have…\n- On a parenting panel I was on recently, one of the participants said she saw our K-12 news on LinkedIn\n- On a customer call, one of our customers mentioned she had read my piece in Forbes\xa0\n- Our landing page for the launch got 1500 page views with no paid marketing\n\nWe didn’t worry about making one big splash and instead just put the product out there and started talking about it. I’m convinced that\'s the way. So check out what we’ve built so far at https://lnkd.in/gTkJKvc8 and stay tuned for lots more to come.', 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '3w', 'last_updated': '2025-06-08 05:25:11', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1061917102, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7312524815859339265', 'followers': 3386, 'date': '1mo', 'description': '🚨 Big news! Winnie is expanding beyond early education — we’re officially launching a K-12 school search: https://lnkd.in/gTJavUxs\n\nWe’re bringing our trusted platform to help families discover all their education options, from preschool through high school.\n\nGet the full scoop on our expansion into K-12 on the latest episode of\xa0Edtech Insiders\xa0This Week in EdTech (Winnie @ 1:04): ht