e to get the message out. I’m now convinced that the days of holding news for the press are over.\n\nHere are some of the ways we got the word out: We submitted a Forbes article related to the launch, I went on the Edtech Insiders podcast, and we announced the news on our own blog and social media channels (including this one right here!). We asked some folks that had email lists and audiences to rebroadcast our news. Soon we’ll be sending out emails to our own audience promoting the expansion to K-12.\n\nSo far it’s been working just as well as any "official press" would have…\n- On a parenting panel I was on recently, one of the participants said she saw our K-12 news on LinkedIn\n- On a customer call, one of our customers mentioned she had read my piece in Forbes\xa0\n- Our landing page for the launch got 1500 page views with no paid marketing\n\nWe didn’t worry about making one big splash and instead just put the product out there and started talking about it. I’m convinced that\'s the way. So check out what we’ve built so far at https://lnkd.in/gTkJKvc8 and stay tuned for lots more to come.', 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '1mo', 'last_updated': '2025-07-08 21:47:42', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1098573397, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7312524815859339265', 'followers': 3422, 'date': '2mo', 'description': '🚨 Big news! Winnie is expanding beyond early education — we’re officially launching a K-12 school search: https://lnkd.in/gTJavUxs\n\nWe’re bringing our trusted platform to help families discover all their education options, from preschool through high school.\n\nGet the full scoop on our expansion into K-12 on the latest episode of\xa0Edtech Insiders\xa0This Week in EdTech (Winnie @ 1:04): https://lnkd.in/gwRpZYCg', 'reactions_count': 11, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-07-08 21:47:42', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1098573398, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7311524609839820800', 'followers': 3422, 'date': '2mo', 'description': 'Winnie on This Week in Edtech!', 'reactions_count': 3, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Alex Sarlin', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/alex-sarlin', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'Discovery Program Lead @ Cambiar Education | Executive MBA', 'reshared_post_description': 'Is China beating the U.S. to AI literacy in schools?\n\nThis Week in Edtech, Ben and I unpack a whirlwind of global AI developments shaking up education and the closure of a key U.S. edtech agency.\n\nFeaturing insights from Annie Chechitelli of Turnitin and Sara Mauskopf of Winnie.\n\n🧠 OpenAI unveils a model focused on creative writing\n\n 📄 Google’s Gemini Canvas & Deep Research tools go free\n\n 💡Zoom’s “Chain of Draft” slashes AI costs by 90%\n\n 🇨🇳 China mandates AI classes for 6-year-olds\n\n 🏛️ U.S. Dept. of EdTech is shut down\n\n 🎓 Turnitin launches “Clarity” to support ethical AI use in classrooms\n\n 🏫 Winnie expands from early ed into K–12 school search\n\nListen to the episode here: https://lnkd.in/eHw8uSjv\n\nStay updated with the latest EdTech news and innovations! Follow Edtech Insiders on 👇\n\nApple Podcasts: https://lnkd.in/gH_ThnJj\nSpotify: https://lnkd.in/eVBaGRVZ\nAmazon Music: https://lnkd.in/gagwAxfX\nSubstack: https://lnkd.in/g2Hs5QGe\nAnd here on LinkedIn!: https://lnkd.in/eNMS5HXU\n\n#EdtechNews\n\nSarah M. Jen Lapaz', 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '2mo', 'last_updated': '2025-07-08 21:47:42', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1098573399, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7305218790366027776', 'followers': None, 'date': '2mo', 'description': 'In a recent Forbes article, Sara Mauskopf underscores the growing demand for providers to deliver more than just daycare. “With parents becoming more selective and competition among [childcare] providers increasing, standing out requires more than just having open spots—it demands differentiation, strong marketing and a commitment to delivering high-quality education.”\n\xa0\nToday’s parents are more discerning than ever. They’re looking for intentional learning environments that set them up for success.\n\xa0\nLearning Care Group is embracing this shift. We focus on early childhood learning and education, offering a research-backed curriculum designed to foster cognitive, social, and emotional growth. We’re working to ensure every child leaves our program not just ready for kindergarten, but ready for life.\n\xa0\nRead Sara Mauskopf’s full article here:', 'reactions_count': 87, 'comments_count': 4, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-07-08 21:47:42', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1098573400, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7302790202194898945', 'followers': 3422, 'date': '3mo', 'description': None, 'reactions_count': 8, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': "AI is transforming industries at an unprecedented pace. We see it writing code, streamlining operations, and even making complex decisions. But amidst all the well deserved hype, one thing is becoming even clearer: the roles that require humans are more valuable than ever.\n\nChildcare and early education are prime examples. While AI can help providers, it cannot replace them. Teaching, nurturing, and fostering social-emotional growth in young children requires a physical human presence. \n\nI shared this as one of 30 leaders of the care economy who contributed to The Holding Co.'s 2025 Care Trends: https://lnkd.in/gK7igMYk  This report combines insight from founders, investors, public sector leaders, and more on what’s happening in care today. The section in AI is one I find particularly interesting.\n\nAs more industries embrace AI, we’ll see a shift in how society values work. I believe jobs that require interpersonal relationships will not only remain irreplaceable but will become more respected and better compensated as their scarcity and importance grow. \n\nAt Winnie, we see firsthand how essential childcare providers are as both educators and as the foundation that enables parents to work and economies to function. As AI reshapes the future of work, I'm hopeful we will recognize and invest in the people who do the jobs that AI never can.", 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '3mo', 'last_updated': '2025-07-08 21:47:42', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1098573401, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7302472846671237120', 'followers': 47848, 'date': '3mo', 'description': 'What was once a supply-constrained market where any open spot would be taken is now demand-driven, where providers compete to stand out. Read more: https://hubs.li/Q038ZvQM0\n\nPost written by Sara Mauskopf, Forbes Councils Member.', 'reactions_count': 13, 'comments_count': 2, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-07-08 21:47:42', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1098573402, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7293006872582701056', 'followers': 163, 'date': '4mo', 'description': 'Here at EarlyJ, we keep our finger on the pulse of current trends in early childhood education. That’s why we were thrilled to recently host a webinar with Sara Mauskopf, CEO and Co-founder of Winnie — a platform that helps millions of parents discover high-quality daycare and preschool optio