vation Summit.\n\nWe started this company over 8 years ago when everyone said the TAM was too small and our idea was too niche. Our “niche company” has the attention of the US government now. LFG!', 'reactions_count': 206, 'comments_count': 16, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2024-11-04 02:38:56', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 764382292, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7190871841643663360', 'followers': None, 'date': '5mo', 'description': 'Price transparency increases enrollment rates by 33% for childcare centers!', 'reactions_count': 22, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': "Imagine not knowing the rent for an apartment until you showed up and toured it. One thing child care providers get wrong is that it's better to withhold any pricing information until a parent tours their center. We have data from Winnie to show that keeping prices a secret is hurting childcare businesses by increasing operational costs and lowering enrollment rates. \n\nIn the competitive world of childcare, transparency isn't just a good practice—it's a strategic advantage. Sharing pricing upfront not only improves search rankings and increases parental interest, but it also leads to a 33% increase in enrollment rates for centers that do so. \n\nIt's an outdated practice to keep prices hidden and it's disadvantaging the entire childcare industry as well as families. Hopefully by sharing the business impact we can advocate for more price transparency in childcare https://lnkd.in/gCgAaHj6", 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '5mo', 'last_updated': '2024-11-04 02:38:56', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 764382293, 'c