t really is when moms simultaneously take a pay cut just as they need to pay for care. https://lnkd.in/gnhRFWVY", 'reactions_count': 160, 'comments_count': 6, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-03-07 18:22:13', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 952555596, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7212083296418062336', 'followers': None, 'date': '8mo', 'description': 'What an honor to be invited to the US Chamber of Commerce today on behalf of Winnie for the first National Child Care Innovation Summit.\n\nWe started this company over 8 years ago when everyone said the TAM was too small and our idea was too niche. Our “niche company” has the attention of the US government now. LFG!', 'reactions_count': 206, 'comments_count': 16, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-03-07 18:22:13', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 962176544, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7302790202194898945', 'followers': 2851, 'date': '2d', 'description': None, 'reactions_count': 5, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': "AI is transforming industries at an unprecedented pace. We see it writing code, streamlining operations, and even making complex decisions. But amidst all the well deserved hype, one thing is becoming even clearer: the roles that require humans are more valuable than ever.\n\nChildcare and early education are prime examples. While AI can help providers, it cannot replace them. Teaching, nurturing, and fostering social-emotional growth in young children requires a physical human presence. \n\nI shared this as one of 30 leaders of the care economy who contributed to The Holding Co.'s 2025 Care Trends: https://lnkd.in/gK7igMYk  This report combines insight from founders, investors, public sector leaders, and more on what’s happening in care today. The section in AI is one I find particularly interesting.\n\nAs more industries embrace AI, we’ll see a shift in how society values work. I believe jobs that require interpersonal relationships will not only remain irreplaceable but will become more respected and better compensated as their scarcity and importance grow. \n\nAt Winnie, we see firsthand how essential childcare providers are as both educators and as the foundation that enables parents to work and economies to function. As AI reshapes the future of work, I'm hopeful we will recognize and invest in the people who do the jobs that AI never can.", 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '2d', 'last_updated': '2025-04-20 23:19:09', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 962176545, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7302472846671237120', 'followers': 45841, 'date': '4d', 'description': 'What was once a supply-constrained market where any open spot would be taken is now demand-driven, where providers compete to stand out. Read more: https://hubs.li/Q038ZvQM0\n\nPost written by Sara Mauskopf, Forbes Councils Member.', 'reactions_count': 10, 'comments_count': 2, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-04-20 23:19:09', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 962176546, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7293006872582701056', 'followers': 111, 'date': '1mo', 'description': 'Here at EarlyJ, we keep our finger on the pulse of current trends in early childhood education. That’s why we were thrilled to recently host a webinar with Sara Mauskopf, CEO and Co-founder of Winnie — a platform that helps millions of parents discover high-quality daycare and preschool options and empowers preschool providers with the tools to grow their businesses. Sara spoke with Bay Area Jewish preschools about how to harness market trends and technology to improve their programming and strengthen their business models. Thank you, Sara, for sharing your expertise! We look forward to hosting more events in response to our local preschools’ needs.\n\n#BayArea #EarlyJ #Impact #NonProfit #JewishEducation #JewishCommunity #JewishNonProfit #EarlyChildhoodEducation #Education #CommunityEngagement #JewishCommunity #Webinar', 'reactions_count': 14, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-04-20 23:19:09', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 962176547, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7288259848893280257', 'followers': 817, 'date': '1mo', 'description': "As a network of Early Childhood Education professionals, there's one truth we've learned: different generations have different childcare needs. What are the needs of Millennial and Gen Z parents? What can we do as providers to meet these needs? \n\nIt was a pleasure to sit down with Sara Mauskopf, CEO and Co-Founder of Winnie, to discuss the shifting needs of today's parents and how childcare providers can meet them: https://bit.ly/4g0sGmt\n\n#ECE #Childcare", 'reactions_count': 11, 'comments_count': 1, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-04-20 23:19:09', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 962176548, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7279990699620495360', 'followers': 2851, 'date': '2mo', 'description': 'This year Winnie helped a record number of families find the childcare they need! Over 659K parents found child care on Winnie with 153K different child care providers across the United States. \n\nTo put this in perspective, there are\xa013.7M households\xa0with children under 6 in the United States.\xa063% of these households\xa0have all parents in the workforce\xa0which means there are 8.6M potential buyers of childcare. Of these families,\xa035% use no form of paid childcare\xa0which leaves us with 6M households paying for childcare in 2024 in the US. We helped place over 10% of these households with their childcare arrangement!\n\nHere’s a sneak peak into what’s ahead in 2025 https://lnkd.in/g3PmFaiU', 'reactions_count': 10, 'comments_count': 1, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-04-20 23:19:09', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 962176549, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7237911245759074306', 'followers': None, 'date': '6mo', 'description': "Trump was recently asked (by Reshma Saujani of Moms First!!) how he was going to make childcare more affordable for families. He gave a word salad of an answer about taxing foreign nations, and his daughter Ivanka, and other stuff that made no sense. So I've fixed it for him. Both Trump and Harris should feel free to use my answer at the upcoming debate as childcare is a bipartisan issue.\n\nFirst, expand the Child Tax Credit. Giving more money to families will help them afford the high prices especially during a child's first five years of life. (Wondering just how much it costs? Check out Winnie's cost calculator at winnie.com/cost-calculator)\n\nSecond, give more funding to child care providers. Child care providers run very low margin businesses and don't get much/any government support the way schools do. Some relief funding like what was provided during the pandemic would go a long way.\n\nFinally, just reduce the amount of regulation that exists in child care. In the state of California, for example, to be a preschool teacher you need an Associate's/Bachelor's Degree plus at least 12 semester units of coursework in early childhood education. That is really expensive and takes years to get. There's also a lot of regulation associated with opening and running a childcare business that doesn't actually make the business any safer but sure is expensive.\n\nThose are just a few ideas. What are yours?", 'reactions_count': 99, 'comments_count': 9, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-04-20 23:19:09', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 962176550, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7227348190545465344', 'followers': None, 'date': '7mo', 'description': "Still pinching myself! Yesterday, on Moms Equal Pay Day, a small group of us gathered with the First Partner of California, Jennifer Siebel Newsom, to talk openly and honestly about how to best support women in the workplace. \n\nWe met on the site of Guidepost Montessori of Emeryville, a beautiful campus caring for kids from 12 weeks to 6 years old - the perfect spot to talk about the importance of childcare and how it's critical infrastructure for mothers and families.\n\nI left the discussion feeling so invigorated. First, it was awesome to hear about how Guidepost has built so many thriving childcare centers (~150!) across the country and world. The news contains so much doom and gloom about the childcare industry but here's a model that supports families, teachers, and provides a great foundation for children. So many awesome businesses like this exist and are thriving!\n\nSecond, it was great to get so much support from the public sector. I was told by the First Partner how much California values innovation in the private sector and how much the govenor's office wants to collaborate with Winnie and see the company thrive. Wow that felt good!", 'reactions_count': 76, 'comments_count': 3, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-04-20 23:19:09', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138590, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7318996802345517056', 'followers': 2989, 'date': '2d', 'description': 'Behind the scenes of our expansion to K-12 school search 👀', 'reactions_count': 3, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': 'I posted a month ago about having trouble getting press for a big launch we had coming up of Winnie\'s K-12 school search. Based on the advice of many of you, we decided to shift gears and instead just use channels we had available to get the message out. I’m now convinced that the days of holding news for the press are over.\n\nHere are some of the ways we got the word out: We submitted a Forbes article related to the launch, I went on the Edtech Insiders podcast, and we announced the news on our own blog and social media channels (including this one right here!). We asked some folks that had email lists and audiences to rebroadcast our news. Soon we’ll be sending out emails to our own audience promoting the expansion to K-12.\n\nSo far it’s been working just as well as any "official press" would have…\n- On a parenting panel I was on recently, one of the participants said she saw our K-12 news on LinkedIn\n- On a customer call, one of our customers mentioned she had read my piece in Forbes\xa0\n- Our landing page for the launch got 1500 page views with no paid marketing\n\nWe didn’t worry about making one big splash and instead just put the product out there and started talking about it. I’m convinced that\'s the way. So check out what we’ve built so far at https://lnkd.in/gTkJKvc8 and stay tuned for lots more to come.', 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '2d', 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138591, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7312524815859339265', 'followers': 2989, 'date': '2w', 'description': '🚨 Big news! Winnie is expanding beyond early education — we’re officially launching a K-12 school search: https://lnkd.in/gTJavUxs\n\nWe’re bringing our trusted platform to help families discover all their education options, from preschool through high school.\n\nGet the full scoop on our expansion into K-12 on the latest episode of\xa0Edtech Insiders\xa0This Week in EdTech (Winnie @ 1:04): https://lnkd.in/gwRpZYCg', 'reactions_count': 11, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-05-13 22:17:46', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1021138592, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7311524609839820800', 'followers': 2989, 'date': '3w', 'description': 'Winnie on This Week in Edtech!', 'reactions_count': 3, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Alex Sarlin', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/alex-sarlin', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'Discovery Program Lead @ Cambiar Education | Executive MBA', 'reshared_post_description': 'Is China beating the U.S. to AI literacy in schools?\n\nThis Week in Edtech, Ben and I unpack a whirlwind of global AI developments shaking up education and the closure of a key U.S. edtech agency.\n\nFeaturing insights from Annie Chechitelli of Turnitin and Sara Mauskopf of Winnie.\n\n🧠 OpenAI 