ityEngagement #JewishCommunity #Webinar', 'reactions_count': 15, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-08-02 13:43:31', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1147961282, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7288259848893280257', 'followers': 837, 'date': '5mo', 'description': "As a network of Early Childhood Education professionals, there's one truth we've learned: different generations have different childcare needs. What are the needs of Millennial and Gen Z parents? What can we do as providers to meet these needs? \n\nIt was a pleasure to sit down with Sara Mauskopf, CEO and Co-Founder of Winnie, to discuss the shifting needs of today's parents and how childcare providers can meet them: https://bit.ly/4g0sGmt\n\n#ECE #Childcare", 'reactions_count': 11, 'comments_count': 1, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-08-02 13:43:31', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1184416129, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7353124417931022336', 'followers': 3600, 'date': '1w', 'description': 'We loved visiting your incredible school 🥰', 'reactions_count': 5, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Alexa Trippensee', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexatrippensee', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'Education Leader - Talent Developer - Process Optimization Enthusiast', 'reshared_post_description': 'What an honor it was to have the pleasure of meeting Annie Trevino finally in person from Winnie !!! We had such a great time touring our BB Country Day School in Pompano Beach, FL and discussing how we will grow together in the future! Thank you for visiting us! We are so thankful for Winnie and Annie’s partnership for our schools.', 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': '2w', 'last_updated': '2025-08-10 15:19:36', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1184416130, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7336814781602926595', 'followers': 836, 'date': '1mo', 'description': "Whole industries are being transformed by AI. While it's true that the #Earlychildhoodeducation field will likely look different as a result of this technology, AI will never be able to replace #ECE professionals. Check out this insightful exploration of the unique importance of educators in the #childcare space by Winnie: https://bit.ly/4d2HIbx", 'reactions_count': 4, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-08-10 15:19:36', 'deleted': 1}, {'id': 1184416131, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7323517852173393921', 'followers': None, 'date': '3mo', 'description': "Mark Zuckerberg is the subject of some outrage. This time he’s in the news for shutting down The Primary School, a free school for low-income Bay Area families, just a few miles from Meta HQ. It offered preschool through 8th grade.\n\nI don’t usually pay close attention to drama around billionaire tech titans, but this one hit differently. A school is closing. Hundreds of families are affected. Zuckerberg called it an experiment that didn’t work out.\n\nExperiments fail all the time in tech. We A/B test, we iterate, we move on. But children aren’t experiments. When kids are in the balance, we don’t get to just walk away.\n\nThis is why the work we’re doing at Winnie takes time. We’ve been at it for almost a decade. I see others in this space raising big capital and trying to scale fast. Too often, families and educators are left behind when the model doesn't work.\n\nWe’re in this for the long haul. Kids and families deserve more than short-term experiments.", 'reactions_count': 1105, 'comments_count': 84, 'reshared_post_author': None, 'reshared_post_author_url': None, 'reshared_post_author_headline': None, 'reshared_post_description': None, 'reshared_post_followers': None, 'reshared_post_date': None, 'last_updated': '2025-08-10 15:19:36', 'deleted': 0}, {'id': 1184416132, 'company_id': 9752392, 'urn': 'urn:li:activity:7318996802345517056', 'followers': 3600, 'date': '3mo', 'description': 'Behind the scenes of our expansion to K-12 school search 👀', 'reactions_count': 11, 'comments_count': None, 'reshared_post_author': 'Sara Mauskopf', 'reshared_post_author_url': 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/smausk', 'reshared_post_author_headline': 'CEO and Co-Founder, Winnie', 'reshared_post_description': 'I posted a month ago about having trouble getting press for a big launch we had coming up of Winnie\'s K-12 school search. Based on the advice of many of you, we decided to shift gears and instead just use channels we had available to get the message out. I’m now convinced that the days of holding news for the press are over.\n\nHere are some of the ways we got the word out: We submitted a Forbes article related to the launch, I went on the Edtech Insiders podcast, and we announced the news on our own blog and social media channels (including this one right here!). We asked some folks that had email lists and audiences to rebroadcast our news. Soon we’ll be sending out emails to our own audience promoting the expansion to K-12.\n\nSo far it’s been working just as well as any "official press" would have…\n- On a parenting panel I was on recently, one of the participants said she saw our K-12 news on LinkedIn\n- On a customer call, one of our customers mentioned she had read my piece in Forbes\xa0\n- Our landing page for the launch got 1500 page views with no paid marketing\n\nWe didn’t worry about making one big splash and instead just put the product out there 